MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Echo displays feel like useful additions to my home viewing and security setup: I could use Alexa controls and potentially view my cameras if they are compatible.",
    "The Echo Show 8 is my strongest choice because its larger screen suits viewing better than the Show 5, while the Dot and smart plug have related appeal but less immediate purpose for me."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The HD and older Fire TV Sticks repeat something my existing 4K Stick already does, with no clear improvement for my 4K TV.",
    "The HDMI cable, 16TB drive, and Wi-Fi extender relate to equipment I own, but I have no current cable shortage, large storage need, or coverage problem. Echo Auto takes Alexa into the car when my interest is in home viewing and security."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Owning Fire TV devices seems to have been taken as a reason to offer more streaming sticks, even though I already have a suitable one.",
    "My interest in connected home equipment seems to have been stretched into interest in nearly any Alexa device or electronics accessory, without a specific use for it."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "What I already own matters: an addition that gives me a useful new capability is more appealing than another device that duplicates my setup.",
    "I need a concrete use before buying. A larger display for possible camera viewing interests me, but camera compatibility matters; automation, storage, and networking purchases need a problem to solve."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You recognized my interest in home viewing, security, and Alexa, but missed the distinction between a useful addition and related equipment I do not currently need."
}
